[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933357322","pull_request_review_id":3946504468,"id":2933357322,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6u13sK","diff_hunk":"@@ -3577,6 +3581,7 @@ void Window::_bind_methods() {\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"dpi_changed\"));\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"titlebar_changed\"));\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"title_changed\"));\n+\tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"hdr_output_changed\"));","path":"scene/main/window.cpp","commit_id":"0a3cc2965c7bbcaadc43181e5712c643c407d76a","original_commit_id":"ba2f6d5c126e639aa104744c204edf81a85ec64a","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ideally constant names may be understood without referring to documentation. Without looking at the documentation, I expect that some users may understand HDR_OUTPUT_CHANGED to be only sent when the `DisplayServer.window_is_hdr_output_enabled` state changes.\n\nMaybe there's a slightly better name that gives more of a hint that this is specifically related to any reason that `Window.get_output_max_linear_value()` has changed. Here are some ideas:\n\n```suggestion\n\tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"output_max_linear_value_changed\"));\n```\n\n```suggestion\n\tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"output_dynamic_range_changed\"));\n```\n\nConstants would also need updating to the new name, of course.","created_at":"2026-03-13T19:31:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T20:10:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933357322","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933357322"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933357322"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933357322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":3584,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":15,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933429486","pull_request_review_id":3946504468,"id":2933429486,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6u2JTu","diff_hunk":"@@ -851,6 +851,11 @@\n \t\t\t\tEmitted when a go back request is sent (e.g. pressing the \"Back\" button on Android), right after [constant Node.NOTIFICATION_WM_GO_BACK_REQUEST].\n \t\t\t</description>\n \t\t</signal>\n+\t\t<signal name=\"hdr_output_changed\">\n+\t\t\t<description>\n+\t\t\t\tEmitted when the HDR output state of the [Window] changes (when HDR output is enabled or disabled, display capabilities change, or system settings are modified).","path":"doc/classes/Window.xml","commit_id":"0a3cc2965c7bbcaadc43181e5712c643c407d76a","original_commit_id":"ba2f6d5c126e639aa104744c204edf81a85ec64a","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Given that users will generally be most interested in having a signal for changes to the output max linear value, I suggest putting the documentation's emphasis on this value with a linked reference to it.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\t\tEmitted when the output max linear value returned by [method Window.get_output_max_linear_value] has changed. This occurs when HDR output is enabled or disabled and when any HDR output luminance values of the window have changed, such as when the player adjusts their screen brightness setting or moves the window to a different screen.\n```\n\nThis would also need to be copied to the other documentation spots.","created_at":"2026-03-13T19:49:38Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T20:10:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933429486","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933429486"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933429486"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933429486/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":856,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933506726","pull_request_review_id":3946504468,"id":2933506726,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6u2cKm","diff_hunk":"","path":"doc/classes/Window.xml","commit_id":"ba2f6d5c126e639aa104744c204edf81a85ec64a","original_commit_id":"ba2f6d5c126e639aa104744c204edf81a85ec64a","user":{"login":"allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp","html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"```suggestion\nReturns the maximum value for linear color components that can be displayed in this window, regardless of SDR or HDR output. Returns [code]1.0[/code] if HDR is not enabled or not supported. The [signal hdr_output_changed] signal will be emitted whenever this value changes.\nThis value is used by tonemapping and other [Environment] effects to ensure that bright colors are presented in the range that can be displayed by this window. When using the Linear tonemapper without [Environment] effects or no [WorldEnvironment], use the returned value to scale content to maximize the screen's brightness, such as for lasers or other bright effects. The following is an example that produces the brightest purple color that the screen can produce:\n```","created_at":"2026-03-13T20:08:39Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T20:10:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933506726","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933506726"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115666#discussion_r2933506726"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115666"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2933506726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":126,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":127,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2970275973","pull_request_review_id":3986854991,"id":2970275973,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6xCtCF","diff_hunk":"@@ -3577,6 +3581,7 @@ void Window::_bind_methods() {\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"dpi_changed\"));\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"titlebar_changed\"));\n \tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"title_changed\"));\n+\tADD_SIGNAL(MethodInfo(\"hdr_output_changed\"));","path":"scene/main/window.cpp","commit_id":"0a3cc2965c7bbcaadc43181e5712c643c407d76a","original_commit_id":"ba2f6d5c126e639aa104744c204edf81a85ec64a","user":{"login":"DarkKilauea","id":1929107,"node_id":